message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Anchored Integrity and Automated Containment for Clinical Record Stores"
authors:
  - family-names: Rayhan
    given-names: Md. Waliul Islam
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Jagannath University, Dhaka, Bangladesh"
    email: waliulrayhan@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-account>/<your-repo>"
keywords:
  - clinical data integrity
  - tamper-evident logging
  - external timestamping
  - RFC 3161
  - RFC 6962
  - automated containment
  - healthcare security
abstract: >
  Prototype and measurement scripts for a clinical record store whose containment response rests on
  a Merkle root published to an external RFC 3161 time-stamping authority, with containment triggered
  by cryptographic mismatch against the published root.
